tci
------------------------------------------
TCI is an interface for creating and organizing teams of threads. It uses a
communicator model, similar to MPI, where threads synchronize and share data
through a handle (the communicator) to a shared state object (the context).
Communicators may be split into smaller sub-communicators for hierarchical
parallelism, with independent synchronization and communication.

Runtime requirements:
  cygwin-3.6.12-1
  libgomp1-14.4.0-1
  libtci-devel-1.0+git20260806-1bl1
  libtci0-1.0+git20260806-1bl1
  pkg-config-3.0.10-1

Build requirements:
(besides corresponding -devel packages)
  binutils-2.47-1
  cmake-4.4.5-1
  cygport-0.37.12-1
  gcc-core-14.4.0-1
  ninja-1.13.2-1

Canonical website:
  https://github.com/MatthewsResearchGroup/tci

Canonical download:
  https://github.com/MatthewsResearchGroup/tci.git

-------------------------------------------

Build instructions:
  1. unpack tci-1.0+git20260806-X-src.tar.xz
  2. if you use setup to install this src package,
     it will be unpacked under /usr/src automatically
        % cd /usr/src
        % cygport ./tci-1.0+git20260806-X.cygport all

This will create:
  /usr/src/tci-1.0+git20260806-X-src.tar.xz
  /usr/src/tci-1.0+git20260806-X.tar.xz
  /usr/src/libtci0-1.0+git20260806-X.tar.xz
  /usr/src/libtci-devel-1.0+git20260806-X.tar.xz

-------------------------------------------

